    {
      "label": "custom_fileless_record",
      "comment": "A REGISTERED CUSTOM COLLECTOR'S RECORD, in the shape that family actually emits: no file path and no language, because a custom node's file path is an optional annotation rather than the unit it is emitted in. It hashes through the SAME fourteen-field tuple the code family uses \u2014 the tuple is not widened for custom graphs \u2014 so eleven of the fourteen fields encode ABSENT and the digest is a function of type, symbol_name and content alone. It is here because the node key made this shape a manifest ENTRY: under the file key it was outside the manifest entirely and no hash of it was ever compared across the two implementations.",
      "kind": "nodes",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "custom-fileless",
          "type": "issue",
          "symbol_name": "ACME-1",
          "file_path": null,
